  "title": "Ce qui a été proposé",
  "titleEn": "What was proposed",
  "level": "B1",
  "minutes": 6,
  "summary": "Nadia writes a careful meeting summary that separates a confirmed decision from an idea still under discussion.",
  "unit": "b1-u07",
  "sentences": [
    {
      "fr": "Après une rencontre sur les activités du centre, Nadia devait envoyer un compte rendu aux membres.",
      "en": "After a meeting about centre activities, Nadia had to send the members a summary."
    },
    {
      "fr": "La responsable a confirmé que la prochaine séance aurait lieu le 14 octobre.",
      "en": "The coordinator confirmed that the next session would take place on October 14."
    },
    {
      "fr": "Un participant a suggéré d'ajouter une activité le samedi, car plusieurs personnes travaillaient le soir.",
      "en": "One participant suggested adding a Saturday activity because several people worked in the evening."
    },
    {
      "fr": "Une autre personne a demandé si le centre pouvait aussi proposer une option en ligne.",
      "en": "Another person asked whether the centre could also offer an online option."
    },
    {
      "fr": "La responsable a répondu que l'équipe examinerait les deux idées avant la prochaine réunion.",
      "en": "The coordinator replied that the team would examine both ideas before the next meeting."
    },
    {
      "fr": "Nadia a écrit que la date était confirmée, mais que les nouveaux formats restaient à l'étude.",
      "en": "Nadia wrote that the date was confirmed, but the new formats were still being considered.",
      "note": "In a summary, attribute proposals to the person who made them and label decisions only when they are confirmed."
    },
    {
      "fr": "Elle a relu son texte pour ne pas présenter une suggestion comme une décision officielle.",
      "en": "She reread her text to avoid presenting a suggestion as an official decision."
    }
  ],
